Plus /metrics endpoint for Prometheus scraping.

Overwrites - Three options:

Error - Refuse if prefix exists, require --force or --continue
Continue - Pick up from existing state (most useful)
Namespace - Auto-suffix like app-20240115 (confusing)
I lean toward continue by default with --fresh to start clean.

Page cleanup - Yes. Two modes:


[retention]
mode = "snapshot"   # Delete WAL older than oldest snapshot (no PITR)
# or
mode = "pitr"       # Keep WAL for point-in-time restore window
pitr_window = "7d"  # How far back you can restore
Wildcard sync - Essential for multi-tenant:


walsync watch "/data/tenants/*.db" --bucket s3://backups
Trigger hierarchy command - Love it:


$ walsync explain --config walsync.toml

Sync triggers (whichever first):
  • 100 changes
  • 10s elapsed
  
Snapshot triggers (whichever first):
  • Every 1h
  • 5m idle
  
Current state:
  • app.db: 34 changes, 6s since sync → sync in 4s
  • users.db: 2 changes, 8s since sync → sync in 2s
